WEBVTT

00:03.002 --> 00:05.754
<i>Causes of death are many and varied.</i>

00:05.755 --> 00:09.425
<i>Old age, suicide, illness...</i>

00:09.426 --> 00:14.180
<i>But the cause of death that scares
the most people in this day and age...</i>

00:18.184 --> 00:19.769
<i>...is death by fire.</i>

02:10.964 --> 02:12.381
<i>Orichalcum.</i>

02:12.382 --> 02:16.678
<i>A legendary ore from
the legendary island, Atlantis.</i>

02:17.679 --> 02:19.888
<i>It's a rock that's amazing
enough to be legendary,</i>

02:19.889 --> 02:21.557
<i>so it's probably really rare.</i>

02:21.558 --> 02:26.271
<i>It's perfect to forge
the legendary sword, Excalibur.</i>

02:26.855 --> 02:28.815
<i>To forge Excalibur,</i>

02:29.816 --> 02:32.360
<i>only orichalcum will do!</i>

02:36.906 --> 02:38.866
Everything is drawn here on this map.

02:38.867 --> 02:41.118
It is dark beneath the lamp post.

02:41.119 --> 02:44.454
The meaning is written in ancient runes,
so I can't understand it,

02:44.455 --> 02:45.622
but "dark"...

02:45.623 --> 02:48.292
This is all that I need to read to know.

02:48.293 --> 02:51.086
If there is anywhere
that's dark, it's the Nether.

02:51.087 --> 02:53.171
The orichalcum is in the Nether!

02:53.172 --> 02:57.050
Doesn't it say it's in
the first shop you visited?

02:57.051 --> 02:58.677
Like the pickle shop?

02:58.678 --> 03:01.388
How could I possibly remember
a place I have never been before?

03:01.389 --> 03:07.228
This is a reference to the land of the
beginning, Atlantis! That's what I think!

03:07.937 --> 03:10.355
That's just what you think.

03:10.356 --> 03:13.025
Yu, he's already revved to full throttle.

03:13.026 --> 03:15.403
At this point, we have to change plans.

03:16.404 --> 03:18.697
Onward, to the Nether!

03:18.698 --> 03:20.575
Y-Yeah...

03:25.288 --> 03:30.500
Fire Force man, my cat climbed
a tree and can't get back down!

03:30.501 --> 03:31.960
Save him!

03:31.961 --> 03:33.962
I'm doing the main quest right now.

03:33.963 --> 03:35.756
I'll do the side quests later.

03:35.757 --> 03:36.840
Farewell!

03:36.841 --> 03:37.967
What?!

03:41.804 --> 03:45.933
You see, Yu, idiots are like
electricity in a short circuit.

03:45.934 --> 03:48.560
They go straight for their goals
without a single thought.

03:48.561 --> 03:49.937
It seems so.

03:49.938 --> 03:54.900
Do you know why I used
the metaphor of a short circuit?

03:54.901 --> 03:56.902
Huh, no I don't.

03:56.903 --> 03:59.154
<i>Do you know what happens when you connect</i>

03:59.155 --> 04:01.865
<i>the positive and negative terminals
of a battery together?</i>

04:01.866 --> 04:03.867
<i>The battery short circuits.</i>

04:03.868 --> 04:06.162
<i>You need to put some kind of
component between them.</i>

04:07.163 --> 04:10.791
Oh, I see. So that's why
you used that metaphor.

04:10.792 --> 04:15.254
Basically, you can't build a machine
with a short circuit.

04:15.255 --> 04:18.215
You need to view things
from every perspective

04:18.216 --> 04:20.384
and find the best way of doing things.

04:20.385 --> 04:22.761
Right! I'll remember that!

04:22.762 --> 04:26.056
This time, you put too much stuff between
the terminals.

04:26.057 --> 04:28.308
He hasn't reached the answer.

04:28.309 --> 04:31.353
I never thought his current was this weak.

04:31.354 --> 04:33.480
It's like a button battery.

04:33.481 --> 04:38.652
But I haven't seen you teach Yu
stuff like this in a long while, Vul.

04:38.653 --> 04:40.321
And me watch you watch him do it.

04:46.035 --> 04:49.664
Even if you short a circuit,
you can always fix it!

04:51.457 --> 04:52.749
What are you doing?

04:52.750 --> 04:55.502
Hurry up and find the
entrance to the Nether.

04:55.503 --> 04:59.674
I need to fix this messed up
situation somehow...

05:04.637 --> 05:07.014
We can enter the Nether from here.

05:07.015 --> 05:09.808
Are you sure we can
go in without permission?

05:09.809 --> 05:13.979
We've done tons of un-Fire-Soldier-like
things on the way here.

05:13.980 --> 05:15.981
There's no turning back now!

05:15.982 --> 05:17.900
Actually, you can. Want to?

05:38.796 --> 05:41.090
We actually entered the Nether...

05:42.091 --> 05:45.302
We said he could turn back,
but he wouldn't listen.

05:45.303 --> 05:48.221
He doesn't listen to
anything we say at all.

05:48.222 --> 05:49.389
At all...

05:49.390 --> 05:50.767
He doesten...

05:51.684 --> 05:53.894
Doesten?! Doesten! Doesten!

05:53.895 --> 05:56.313
Yu's lost his mind
from his fear of the Nether.

05:56.314 --> 05:58.483
It's his first time in
the Nether, after all.

05:59.150 --> 06:00.859
Come to your senses, Yu!

06:00.860 --> 06:02.235
This is the Nether.

06:02.236 --> 06:04.321
If you let down your guard,
the abyss will gaze into you!

06:04.322 --> 06:06.032
Open your eyes!

06:10.328 --> 06:12.162
Knight King Arthur!

06:12.163 --> 06:13.497
What was I...

06:13.498 --> 06:16.416
If you don't keep your wits
about you, it'll take your mind.

06:16.417 --> 06:17.919
Yes! I'll keep them!

06:19.670 --> 06:23.716
Yeah, I know.
What the heck are we even doing?

06:24.383 --> 06:26.385
Lisa, are you okay?

06:27.470 --> 06:30.389
Doesn't the Nether
make you remember the past?

06:33.559 --> 06:35.561
I've got my eyes on the future now.

06:36.646 --> 06:40.398
Sure, I still fear Dr. Giovanni,

06:40.399 --> 06:44.277
but I'm sure that the time will come
when I need to overcome him.

06:44.278 --> 06:46.948
When that time comes,
I'll be there to smash him with you!

06:48.783 --> 06:50.909
We don't have much time
until the Great Cataclysm.

06:50.910 --> 06:53.829
We definitely need Arthur's powers!

06:53.830 --> 06:56.833
That's why we need to
get him to power up now!

06:58.918 --> 07:03.172
But his delusions are
more effective than training...

07:03.840 --> 07:06.633
How the heck do pyrokinetic
powers even work?

07:06.634 --> 07:09.720
What the heck is this Adolla anyway?

07:22.358 --> 07:23.984
Lieutenant Konro.

07:23.985 --> 07:27.737
What're you sitting around in here for?
You're all better, right?

07:27.738 --> 07:28.739
Yes.

07:30.450 --> 07:32.201
Um, Lieutenant Konro...

07:32.952 --> 07:33.952
Hm?

07:33.953 --> 07:37.706
You've experienced
an Adolla Link before, right?

07:37.707 --> 07:39.959
Do you remember how you did it?

07:42.753 --> 07:45.298
I can't just sit around waiting anymore.

07:45.965 --> 07:48.551
I want to charge into Adolla myself.

07:53.431 --> 07:55.807
Vul, are you sure we can get back?

07:55.808 --> 07:59.103
A maze is just like a circuit.
I remember the way.

07:59.770 --> 08:02.439
We've been wandering for over an hour.

08:02.440 --> 08:04.609
Let's let him go until he's had enough.

08:05.234 --> 08:06.985
We pick up some random piece of metal

08:06.986 --> 08:10.406
and switch it out
with the alloy I got for him.

08:11.199 --> 08:15.536
But yeah, going any deeper
into the Nether is dangerous.

08:16.412 --> 08:19.999
All right. I'll make the final boss
appear so we can end it.

08:26.464 --> 08:30.383
Turn back! I am the Ruler of the Abyss!

08:30.384 --> 08:34.180
Orichalcum lies beyond here!
You shall not have it!

08:34.722 --> 08:37.182
Turn back!

08:37.183 --> 08:40.060
Lisa, you're a grown woman.
Stop playing like a child.

08:40.061 --> 08:41.187
Yu's watching.

08:41.812 --> 08:44.272
He's got a weird knack for these things.

08:44.273 --> 08:46.107
I had to fight through embarrassment too.

08:46.108 --> 08:48.401
Don't do anything hasty!

08:48.402 --> 08:50.987
You nearly wrecked the whole
adventure we put him on!

08:50.988 --> 08:53.657
We've been at this for over an hour!

08:53.658 --> 08:56.327
He isn't bored of it yet?! He's a big boy!

08:57.495 --> 08:59.079
Lisa, he's bored.

08:59.080 --> 09:01.248
Ugh! Let me kill him!

09:01.249 --> 09:04.668
You damn stupid dog! Making us
walk you all the way down here!

09:04.669 --> 09:07.254
- Lisa, calm down!
- I'll teach you who's in charge here!

09:07.255 --> 09:08.839
We're doing it to save Tokyo!

09:09.966 --> 09:11.968
Why're you acting all serious now?

09:12.843 --> 09:14.261
I sense a presence.

09:14.262 --> 09:16.888
Oh, please, Arthur. This is the Nether--

09:16.889 --> 09:18.474
Arthur, are you sure?

09:19.058 --> 09:20.059
Stand back.

09:22.144 --> 09:23.020
Who goes there?!

09:35.491 --> 09:37.617
It really is you, Arthur!

09:37.618 --> 09:38.536
It's been a while.

09:39.996 --> 09:42.330
Mother... Father...

09:42.331 --> 09:45.709
Oh, it's just his mother and father?

09:45.710 --> 09:47.295
Phew. Scaring us like that...

09:48.212 --> 09:49.462
What are you doing in this place?

09:49.463 --> 09:51.548
I told you once before, Arthur?

09:51.549 --> 09:52.924
Could it be, Father...

09:52.925 --> 09:54.135
H-Hold up...

09:54.719 --> 09:55.844
Yeah, that's right.

09:55.845 --> 09:57.388
GONE ON A JOURNEY TO SAVE THE WORLD!

09:58.222 --> 10:00.056
You were journeying to save the world!

10:00.057 --> 10:02.601
Did you set this up too, Vulcan?!

10:02.602 --> 10:04.185
You know I didn't!

10:04.186 --> 10:08.648
Nothing less from my father and mother!
Father King and Mother King!

10:08.649 --> 10:10.818
Work worthy of the title of king!

10:11.611 --> 10:15.363
That outfit! You've grown up
to be a Fire Soldier, Arthur!

10:15.364 --> 10:19.160
You were fighting to
save the world, my son!

10:19.744 --> 10:23.956
On the day you left the castle
on your journey, I became Knight King.

10:24.540 --> 10:29.085
Fire Soldier and Knight King.
It was difficult to wear two crowns.

10:29.086 --> 10:30.671
Son...

10:31.756 --> 10:33.173
Oh, how you've grown!

10:33.174 --> 10:35.134
Heh. I am a knight.

10:35.801 --> 10:37.260
Excuse me a sec.

10:37.261 --> 10:41.681
You two are Arthur's parents,
and you were out saving the world?

10:41.682 --> 10:44.476
This make so little sense, I can't follow.

10:44.477 --> 10:47.813
So what's going on?
Could you explain, please?

10:48.397 --> 10:50.815
Vulcan, don't think, feel.

10:50.816 --> 10:53.276
You need to stop feeling and think!

10:53.277 --> 10:56.154
You must be his Fire Soldier friends.

10:56.155 --> 10:58.114
Yeah, that's right.

10:58.115 --> 11:01.327
We're crewmen with
the 8th, just like Arthur.

11:02.328 --> 11:04.329
We are the Resistance!

11:04.330 --> 11:07.708
We work to correct all that
is rotten in this country!

11:08.417 --> 11:10.126
Resistance?

11:10.127 --> 11:12.420
Well, in simple terms,

11:12.421 --> 11:17.384
he came up with this story to escape
from the loan sharks, and I followed it.

11:17.385 --> 11:19.511
Excuse me?! What do you mean?

11:19.512 --> 11:23.598
Basically, we're playing
pretend Resistance in the Nether.

11:23.599 --> 11:26.267
And you've been playing that
in the Nether for years?

11:26.268 --> 11:29.312
Why would you ever
join in his stupid games?!

11:29.313 --> 11:32.857
I couldn't let him go to the Nether alone.

11:32.858 --> 11:37.070
Arthur was a child, so we couldn't
put him in harm's way.

11:37.071 --> 11:39.948
He isn't the best husband,
but I still love him.

11:39.949 --> 11:42.410
And you guys just abandoned Arthur?!

11:45.704 --> 11:48.081
Well thought, Mother. Truly wise.

11:48.082 --> 11:51.709
All that we did was to keep
the world from disaster.

11:51.710 --> 11:53.586
Keep the world from disaster? You--

11:53.587 --> 11:56.840
The Holy Sol Temple which worships

11:56.841 --> 12:00.135
the Great Sol was created
to manipulate the people.

12:00.136 --> 12:03.012
It seems that a higher-dimensional
entity called the Evangelist

12:03.013 --> 12:07.685
wants to recreate the Great Cataclysm
and destroy the world.

12:08.894 --> 12:09.978
How do you know that?

12:09.979 --> 12:13.898
Human combustion occurs when
a copy of yourself in another world

12:13.899 --> 12:16.235
interacts with you in this one.

12:25.995 --> 12:27.078
Hold up!

12:27.079 --> 12:29.789
The Evangelist and another world?!
Where did you hear that?

12:29.790 --> 12:33.669
Where did I hear it?
It's all my husband's delusions.

12:34.378 --> 12:36.337
Old man, how'd you find that out?

12:36.338 --> 12:38.966
I don't know what you want me to say.

12:41.635 --> 12:44.388
Because I'm a prophet.

12:45.598 --> 12:48.808
<i>After our restaurant went under
from food poisoning and a fire</i>

12:48.809 --> 12:51.395
<i>and our finances were a flaming mess...</i>

12:54.648 --> 12:57.818
<i>...all I could do was escape from reality.</i>

13:10.122 --> 13:12.291
Why are you looking inside your hat?

13:13.042 --> 13:14.627
Do you see anything in it?

13:19.882 --> 13:25.262
Arthur, your mother and father are
going on a journey to save the world.

13:26.055 --> 13:27.473
We love you.

13:31.268 --> 13:32.478
Take care.

13:37.816 --> 13:41.904
Ever since that day, whenever I'm
at a loss and look into my hat,

13:42.488 --> 13:45.616
I could see a sky full of stars inside it.

13:46.450 --> 13:48.911
<i>When I'm looking out
at the stars, I can tell.</i>

13:49.453 --> 13:51.038
The truth about this planet.

13:52.039 --> 13:54.707
Arthur, are you sure they're your parents?

13:54.708 --> 13:57.419
Of course they are.
Deception has no effect on me.

13:58.045 --> 13:59.629
How could I mistake anyone else for them?

13:59.630 --> 14:01.297
Vulcan...

14:01.298 --> 14:03.926
He's too on point for coincidence.

14:04.510 --> 14:06.803
Did you appear in front of us
from a prophecy too?

14:06.804 --> 14:08.889
I felt like my son would be here.

14:09.974 --> 14:13.226
Arthur, you came down here
searching for something.

14:13.227 --> 14:15.353
Yes, indeed, Father.

14:15.354 --> 14:19.357
I came here searching for orichalcum
to forge the true Excalibur.

14:19.358 --> 14:20.860
Follow me.

14:26.156 --> 14:28.616
Vul, you're too quick to trust people!

14:28.617 --> 14:31.327
That's why
you fell for my lies right away--

14:31.328 --> 14:32.955
But we're still together now.

14:33.914 --> 14:36.208
W-Well, yeah...

14:42.756 --> 14:45.466
What the heck is this mountain of trash?

14:45.467 --> 14:47.010
I've seen this before all right.

14:47.011 --> 14:47.927
Knight?

14:47.928 --> 14:49.470
I said, "right."

14:49.471 --> 14:52.807
This is technology from before
the Great Cataclysm.

14:52.808 --> 14:54.642
We've collected these machines here.

14:54.643 --> 14:56.645
Huh...

14:57.563 --> 15:01.983
I've never seen this junk before.
Is this some kind of device?

15:01.984 --> 15:04.570
I think it was around here...

15:05.195 --> 15:06.447
Found it.

15:07.907 --> 15:08.949
This is it.

15:09.575 --> 15:10.658
What is this?

15:10.659 --> 15:12.869
Hold on, is that...

15:12.870 --> 15:14.747
A fairing from a space rocket?!

15:15.331 --> 15:16.748
You know about them?

15:16.749 --> 15:20.710
These are made of
a special aluminum alloy.

15:20.711 --> 15:25.757
It's so heat-resistant and sturdy that
2,000 or 3,000 degrees does nothing to it!

15:25.758 --> 15:30.178
Dark matter which floats through space.
You could call it the fragment of a star.

15:30.179 --> 15:31.971
If we forge the Holy Sword of it...

15:31.972 --> 15:33.348
No, it isn't. Weren't you listening?

15:33.349 --> 15:35.476
It's a space rocket part, not a meteor--

15:38.896 --> 15:40.689
He's revved up!

15:43.359 --> 15:46.861
- Who?!
- Dad, Mom!

15:46.862 --> 15:48.947
- We're home!
- Were you good while we were gone?

15:48.948 --> 15:50.907
- Yeah.
- What?! No way! Kids?!

15:50.908 --> 15:52.492
Huh?! How?!

15:52.493 --> 15:53.743
And three of them?!

15:53.744 --> 15:54.661
How?!

15:54.662 --> 15:56.079
We had them after we came to the Nether.

15:56.080 --> 15:58.790
"You had them"? Hold up.

15:58.791 --> 15:59.749
What?!

15:59.750 --> 16:01.125
I mean, you abandoned him!

16:01.126 --> 16:02.669
Yu, it's fine.

16:02.670 --> 16:04.420
Every family has their own reasons.

16:04.421 --> 16:07.632
Hold on! This is just plain wrong!

16:07.633 --> 16:09.092
What about Arthur?

16:09.093 --> 16:10.635
Why'd you make more?!

16:10.636 --> 16:13.347
You abandoned him because you
couldn't bring a kid into the Nether!

16:13.931 --> 16:17.184
How do you think Arthur feels about this?!

16:18.727 --> 16:20.646
Oh good. He wasn't listening.

16:21.730 --> 16:24.816
Arthur! With this baby,
I can forge a better sword

16:24.817 --> 16:26.776
than with that
fakechalcum I set up for you!

16:26.777 --> 16:28.861
Hey! Vulcan! You went and said it!

16:28.862 --> 16:30.279
You said you set it up!

16:30.280 --> 16:33.491
You revealed everything about
all the charades we went through!

16:33.492 --> 16:35.535
Really, Vulcan? We've done it!

16:35.536 --> 16:39.956
Hell yeah! He totally ignores anything
that doesn't fit his narrative!

16:39.957 --> 16:42.041
Aw crap, now I'm totally revved up!

16:42.042 --> 16:43.836
What is wrong with them?

16:44.378 --> 16:47.672
Now, we just get to the surface
and forge that sword.

16:47.673 --> 16:48.881
Let's forge it!

16:48.882 --> 16:51.135
Excalibur!

17:03.105 --> 17:05.940
Well, I'm completely exhausted.

17:05.941 --> 17:08.443
Where's your family now, Arthur?

17:08.444 --> 17:10.320
They haven't been on
the surface in a while.

17:10.946 --> 17:12.156
<i>They're exploring the town.</i>

17:13.240 --> 17:15.409
Everyone in the Boyle family
just does their own thing.

17:16.285 --> 17:21.122
All right, everything's ready.
Next, it's time to pour it into this baby.

17:21.123 --> 17:22.541
I'm watching!

17:28.047 --> 17:29.505
Ooh!

17:29.506 --> 17:31.425
Now this has even got me excited!

17:39.475 --> 17:40.892
Stay back! Stay back!

17:40.893 --> 17:44.729
You might be a third-generation,
but it's still stupid hot up close!

17:44.730 --> 17:47.940
Making a sword out of a rocket
has this feeling of adventure to it.

17:47.941 --> 17:50.402
It was worth the effort.

17:51.361 --> 17:54.823
I've never seen Arthur that happy before.

17:57.159 --> 18:00.120
Come, settle in my hand, Holy Sword!

18:28.524 --> 18:30.858
The sheath will be finished shortly.

18:30.859 --> 18:32.819
The belt to hang it on is done too.

18:32.820 --> 18:35.280
All right! We're almost done here!

18:39.284 --> 18:42.037
Arthur! Come on! Hurry up!

18:42.996 --> 18:44.413
Sorry to keep you waiting.

18:44.414 --> 18:46.708
Feast your eyes on this baby. It's done!

18:58.387 --> 18:59.513
This is...

19:01.682 --> 19:03.809
Vulcan, thank you.

19:05.185 --> 19:06.811
I swear upon this sword

19:06.812 --> 19:10.607
that I will never again lose to anything!

19:11.191 --> 19:13.944
We're counting on you, Knight King!

19:18.574 --> 19:19.908
Arthur!

19:20.576 --> 19:23.620
I heard you found your parents.
That's great news!

19:25.664 --> 19:26.664
What's that?

19:26.665 --> 19:29.041
THE SURFACE WAS FUN. WE'RE GOING ON
ANOTHER JOURNEY. SEE YOU. YOUR FATHER

19:29.042 --> 19:31.253
What? Again?

19:36.049 --> 19:37.967
<i>A thought ran through Maki's mind.</i>

19:37.968 --> 19:40.011
<i>As she looked upon this man,</i>

19:40.012 --> 19:43.515
<i>completely oblivious that he had now
been abandoned by his parents twice,</i>

19:44.099 --> 19:46.767
<i>that he, with the true Holy Sword in hand,</i>

19:46.768 --> 19:49.646
<i>was the Knight King
who would save this planet.</i>

19:54.776 --> 19:57.112
Come on. You've still got
some tension in there.

19:58.614 --> 20:02.575
I asked Lieutenant Konro about
how to establish an Adolla Link...

20:02.576 --> 20:04.577
I heard that from Konro.

20:04.578 --> 20:06.914
You're gonna launch
your own raid on Adolla.

20:07.623 --> 20:11.292
Do you know how to raid Adolla,
Captain Shinmon?

20:11.293 --> 20:12.461
No. Hell no.

20:13.545 --> 20:18.466
But if the Evangelist really is a god,
then I can't say I don't know a way.

20:18.467 --> 20:20.135
Then what we're doing right now...

20:20.802 --> 20:22.221
Your third eye.

20:22.721 --> 20:26.849
If you can open it, you can connect with
the universe and higher dimensions

20:26.850 --> 20:31.104
and finally connect to the
seat of God... or so they say.

20:31.688 --> 20:32.814
Connect to higher dimensions?

20:33.815 --> 20:35.234
<i>Third eye?</i>

20:36.109 --> 20:39.320
What do I need to do to open my third eye?

20:39.321 --> 20:44.450
First, relieve your body of all tension.
Feel the earth in the palms of your hands.

20:44.451 --> 20:46.786
Close your eyes and focus your mind.

20:46.787 --> 20:49.915
Become one with the
earth and quiet yourself.

20:53.085 --> 20:54.962
Become one with the earth...

20:57.506 --> 21:01.133
I never feel anything,
so I always fall fast asleep.

21:01.134 --> 21:02.718
Earth...

21:02.719 --> 21:04.679
Focus mind...

21:04.680 --> 21:07.015
Become one...

21:07.766 --> 21:09.059
Sleep...

21:10.686 --> 21:12.312
Don't sleep, idiot.

21:13.021 --> 21:16.399
My mentor made me do this,
but I never had faith,

21:16.400 --> 21:19.486
so all I did was have
a nice nap every time.

21:20.153 --> 21:21.862
But maybe you--

21:21.863 --> 21:23.365
Of course you wouldn't have faith in it.

21:24.032 --> 21:26.242
Captain Shinmon, you're
the God of Destruction.

21:26.243 --> 21:27.952
People are supposed to have faith in you.

21:27.953 --> 21:30.414
And I have faith in you, Captain Shinmon.

21:31.456 --> 21:33.708
What kind of nonsense is that, kid?

21:33.709 --> 21:34.792
Keep trying.

21:34.793 --> 21:35.919
Yes.

21:36.461 --> 21:38.505
I'm gonna gamble on a game of dice.

22:20.213 --> 22:21.340
Sho!

22:25.927 --> 22:27.054
Who are you?

22:28.805 --> 22:30.307
We finally meet again.

22:38.023 --> 22:39.106
Brother?

22:39.107 --> 22:42.944
TO BE CONTINUED

24:14.452 --> 24:15.411
NEXT TIME

24:15.412 --> 24:18.456
<i>Nothing remains
after the disaster which I cause.</i>

24:19.457 --> 24:22.377
<i>I must meet my brother once again.</i>

24:22.878 --> 24:24.962
<i>Next time, "Advent."</i>

24:24.963 --> 24:27.716
<i>Return to the great flame of fire.</i> Látom.
